  "profile": "https://lloom.dev/profiles/interchange/v1",
  "id": "linux-nvidia-dgx-spark-2x-glm53-atlas",
  "name": "2x DGX Spark GLM-5.3 Flash NVFP4 Atlas",
  "version": 1,
  "summary": "Candidate lane for two directly connected Sparks running Atlas SparkGLM over the private fabric, serving GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 from a once-per-node overlay conversion with 1048576-token contexts for four concurrent requests and DFlash2 speculative decoding. Additive only: no default model, no aliases overwritten.",
  "description": "This recipe installs the Atlas SparkGLM candidate at the immutable product revision recorded in backends/atlas-sparkglm/pins.json. LLooM owns orchestration, admission, worker-first startup, readiness, routing and telemetry. The Atlas engine image is built from Enntity/sparkglm by that repository's install/build.sh; LLooM commits no engine source. The engine (Atlas-Inf/atlas with SparkGLM's work on the Enntity/atlas fork) is AGPL-3.0-only and runs from its own container image, and the DFlash2 drafter weights are CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (non-commercial). Setup acquires the pinned model, pulls the pinned image from GHCR by its immutable manifest digest (image.reference in the pin manifest; the mutable tag is never pulled), performs the overlay conversion, and the serving path only ever starts the prepared image. Each node verifies the pulled image by the io.enntity.sparkglm.install-tree contents label and arm64 architecture; the label is a contents check, not the artifact identity. Explicit --source-build is only for users who want a local build from the pinned source, and it produces a LOCAL tag for an explicitly overridden local recipe, not the immutable recipe. The candidate includes structured output and tool calls plus image/video input; live hardware and full serving qualification remain pending.",
  "license": {
    "id": "MIT",
    "name": "Recipe metadata, launcher and orchestration"
  },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "Atlas SparkGLM candidate at product revision b6bed25903578b4f4ed4f0e7204c80700ad5b8d9 (engine Enntity/atlas sparkglm/atlas-20261009-rc2 @ f2b805e7, AGPL-3.0-only, recorded in the image's /opt/atlas/source-manifest.json; corresponding source is Enntity/sparkglm at that revision plus that Enntity/atlas commit). The normal install path pulls the immutable GHCR manifest digest ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm@sha256:9a583b07912262f08f72d33773c994d2468d5292546e79e149c701962101dbc7; the tag ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm:4046c81baa07 is source-build metadata and is never pulled. Each host verifies the pulled image's io.enntity.sparkglm.install-tree contents label equals install tree 4046c81baa071cb109e55c3206ed1fca3bd3db9a and the image is arm64; the label is a contents check, not an artifact identity. An explicit --source-build builds from Enntity/sparkglm install/ at that revision and produces a LOCAL tag for an explicitly overridden local recipe only, and does not satisfy the normal immutable recipe. Model nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 revision 423acf37583782c51c142d145aef733d72943d93 requires a once-per-node overlay conversion gated on conversion.complete.json plus verification; the DFlash2 drafter incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 revision 7d74cdd881ed7e32c31175984a67823127b66cfe (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, non-commercial) is served from its checkpoint. The engine argument vector ships inside the image as /opt/atlas/profiles/4x1m.json, selected with SPARKGLM_PROFILE=4x1m, not in this recipe. The profile carries 1048576-token contexts, four sequences sharing one physical KV pool (GLM latent in FP8 with per-128 scales, split between the two nodes by SPARKGLM_KV_SHARD=1, qualified at about 2.38M tokens at the recipe's 0.91 GPU memory utilization with the display carveout, which overrides the profile default of 0.88, and shared with the disk prefix cache; the 48 GiB disk prefix-cache tier is enabled beside the shard, split into 24 GiB KV and 24 GiB SSM tiers per node), FP32 SSM state with KDA record rollback, and DFlash2 (gamma 8) on the head rank; disable-tool-grammar is deliberately not set so structured output and tools stay functional."
  },
