  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems",
    "notes": [
      "Candidate lane: no live hardware qualification has been recorded through LLooM yet. The profile and capability claims below come from the source build and focused checks; gateway and two-node serving canaries remain required before treating this recipe as qualified.",
      "TP2 with expert parallelism 2 across the private ConnectX RoCE fabric. The direct-fabric address and NIC are discovered per node and passed as MASTER_ADDR and FABRIC_INTERFACE; no host-specific addresses are pinned.",
      "The worker is admitted first (rank 1) and readiness-checked through its container state, because the Atlas engine has no separate worker HTTP surface. The leader starts second (rank 0) and owns routing.",
      "The NVFP4 checkpoint requires a per-node overlay conversion before it can be served. LLooM treats the conversion as incomplete unless conversion.complete.json plus its recorded verification are present.",
      "Licenses: the Atlas engine in the image is AGPL-3.0-only (Atlas-Inf/atlas with SparkGLM's work on Enntity/atlas; not included in LLooM). The default DFlash2 drafter incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (non-commercial); nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 is MIT per SparkGLM docs/LICENSING.md. Read each model card before use.",
      "Both nodes must carry the same portable source, model and converter pins plus the same backend directory. The normal path addresses the pinned immutable digest (image.reference), so both hosts run the same artifact; each host verifies the pulled image's install-tree contents label and arm64 architecture. An explicit --source-build produces a LOCAL tag for an explicitly overridden local recipe only and does not satisfy the normal immutable recipe; image IDs may differ across such source builds.",
      "Peak container memory is capped at 114 GiB with a 4096 MiB OOM guard. The profile's default GPU memory utilization is 0.88 and the recipe raises it to 0.91 through SPARKGLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION (0.93 left rank 0 under 1 GiB free under real traffic). The KV budget counts weights, workspaces, SSM verify pools and the DFlash drafter; at 0.88, measured host headroom stayed above 8 GiB with four concurrent 190K-token requests. The 4x1m profile serves 1048576-token contexts to four sequences from one shared FP8-latent KV pool that SPARKGLM_KV_SHARD=1 splits between the ranks: about 2.38M tokens at 0.91 (with the GB10 display carveout lent to the KV cache and the disk prefix cache on; a four-session 204K fill left rank 0 at 4.8 GB free at worst), shared with the prefix cache; both ranks agree on the smaller pool. The disk prefix-cache tier (prefixCacheGb 48) runs beside the shard: each node spills and restores only the latents it owns. Configure explicit LLooM utilization 0.97 and reserve 4 GiB on both nodes while keeping enforcement active."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": {
